# Git already stores every text file in this repo with LF. Check them out with
# LF too, on every platform, so the working tree matches the index.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites the working tree to CRLF
# on checkout, and Prettier (endOfLine defaults to "lf") then reports a
# "Delete `CR`" error on every line of every file — ~11,700 phantom lint errors
# that do not exist in the repository and never appear on Linux or in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never apply end-of-line conversion. These all contain CR bytes as
# part of their payload, so an accidental conversion would corrupt them.
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.zip  binary
